- [will_said + observed] PHEXT CHAINING RULING (Will, 07:31): consume 0x02 as the chain delimiter — it separates whole phexts within a chain, one rung above Library (0x01); standoff relationships at scale are encoded across two or more chained phexts, not by embedded markup and not a tenth dimension. Verified first: 0x02 occurs zero times in CYOA, incipit.phext, and emise.phext.
- [will_said + observed] PHEXT CHAIN CLOSE RULING — 0x03, TIME (Will, 07:43): "I agree, codify this as libphext-rs v0.6, We can now encode TIME." 0x03 is consumed as the chain close: it terminates a chain, so completeness is verifiable — a chain ending without 0x03 was truncated; a chain is an ordered series of complete phext states, editions in succession. 0x04 was noted as the last rung — NOT consumed, no ruling.
- [will_said] CHAIN DECISION POINT AND FRAMING (08:03): the decision point is Gerhard Zorn's tweet asking for "phext expressions" / a "phext algebra". Will, verbatim: "I have already been using multiple phexts in various contexts. This enables subspace freedom, and neatly solves the mutable emissary problem." Will's framing (08:05): phext chains are 11D text splats, with standoff-based access to subspace.
